  "title": "Answer: spacetime is one useful model of the emergent world",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "fbdd2e2e-0c39-414c-9d8a-ba7436837e85",
      "text": "Describing the emergent world as a $3+1$-dimensional spacetime, rather than as a simulation on a one-dimensional Turing machine, is a matter of utility, not of differing predictions. Ontological models of the world are never unique.",
